A||||3||FieroGT||84-87 Rear Caliper Rebuild Kits||||10
Z||000000||FieroGT||10-12-1999||09:49 AM||||If anyone has the know-how to rebuild their rear calipers, let me offer a reasonably priced solution. Go to the dealership and order part number 18019027. This is the kit used as per the recall to rebuild the rear calipers. It includes all of the caliper innards, not just the seals. You even get new caliper pistons with this kit. 1 kit includes all parts necessary to rebuild BOTH rear calipers, so all you need is one kit. Retail is somewhere around $57, but you can probably get trade price of about $37 on it if you ask for it. Well worth the money, in my opinion. Just make sure that your bleeder screws aren't frozen or broken before you order the kit. Use plenty of Liquid wrench (or whatever your favorite product is) on them before trying to loosen them.<p>[This message has been edited by FieroGT (edited 10-12-1999).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||ka4nkf||10-12-1999||11:38 AM||||FieroGT<BR>Thanks For The Info On The Brake Re-build Kit. I Have Been Lookinf For That.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-12-1999||01:43 PM||||I use the spray oil. Often that works by itself.<P>If you need a bit more persuasion, a few taps square on the tip of the bleeders with a plastic face hammer can help to. Don't use a metal hammer, not even brass. If you have room tapping while you load them a bit with a 6 point box end wrench often pops them loose.<P>to prevent future contamination and jamming of the bleeders, clean out the holes, and install new bleeders with a Tiny bit of anti sieze worked into the threads. Use as little as posible to avoid contaminating the brake fluid. you just need a film of antisieze on them. After bleeding spray across the tip with air to draw out excess brake fluid. (like blowing across a bottle to make noise.) Then spray into them with some WD 40 or something like that. If posible put caps on the bleeders to keep out crud.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||10-12-1999||03:22 PM||||Yesterday both my front and rear calipers were rebuilt. This was quite an expensive operation (because it took them about 8 hours) but it was well worth it. It cured <B>all</B> problems I had with my brakes and they feel as new again!<P>Brakes are without any doubt the most important part of your car - take good care of them.||||reg||1
